  "live_records": {
    "q-90309": {
      "dom_id": "step-q90309",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈2.2778,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}, & 0<x<2, \\\\ \\frac{7}{9}, & 2\\le x<3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{4}}{12}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{7{x}^{2}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{5}}{60}|}_{0}^{2}+{\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{27}|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & ≈5.4593\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & ≈5.4593-(2.2778)^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.271\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to three decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
