      "problem": "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]≈3.314\\,81,$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{9}, & 0<x<3, \\\\ \\frac{1}{9}(2x-5), & 3\\le x<5, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{5}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}(2x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{1}{9}(2{x}^{3}-5{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{27}|}_{0}^{3}+{\\frac{1}{9}(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{2}-\\frac{5{x}^{3}}{3})|}_{3}^{5} \\\\  & ≈13.074\\,07\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & ≈13.074\\,07-(3.314\\,81)^{2} \\\\  & ≈2.09\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
